Z||000003||rockcrawl||06-27-2001||04:43 PM||||I've determined that there are stock GM axles that will work for putting a 440T4/4T60 trans in a Fiero. 1987 Pontiac 6000, no ABS, light duty brakes. These axles fit perfectly with no mods. A search should reveal the rest of the answers.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ThatRickGuy||06-28-2001||09:15 AM||||anyone w/ the AOD trannys use a different torque converter? I've heard that the AOD TCs are lower RPMs, what about using the stock TH125 TC w/ an AOD tranny? Also, any problems w/ the TC lock up? I thought it depended on the ECM telling it that the tranny is in 3rd gear...<P>Just happened across this. thought people might like to know:<P>Front Wheel Drive <BR>TH-125C (3T40)  2.840  1.600  1.000  2.067 <BR>TH-440T4(4T60)  2.921  1.568  1.000  0.705  2.385 <BR>4T60-E  2.921  1.568  1.000  0.705  2.385 <BR>4T65-E  2.921  1.568  1.000  0.705  2.385 <BR>4T80-E  2.960  1.626  1.000  0.681  2.130 <BR><p>[This message has been edited by ThatRickGuy (edited 06-28-2001).]||||reg||1
